1. Superpowers — instruction text copied verbatim
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

craft's SDLC commands and doctrine files incorporate instruction text copied,
in places verbatim, from the Superpowers plugin.

    Project:  Superpowers (https://github.com/obra/superpowers)
    Author:   Jesse Vincent
    Version:  5.0.7  (pinned — craft does not track upstream)
    License:  MIT

Material is derived from these skills:

    brainstorming/SKILL.md                  → commands/craft-explore.md
    writing-plans/SKILL.md                  → commands/craft-propose.md
    test-driven-development/SKILL.md        → doctrine/tdd.md
    systematic-debugging/SKILL.md           → doctrine/debugging.md
    verification-before-completion/SKILL.md → doctrine/verification.md
    executing-plans/SKILL.md                → commands/craft-apply.md

Certain passages are reproduced verbatim by deliberate design rather than
convenience: their value lies in exact wording that forecloses rationalisation
(the Iron Law blocks, "Red Flags — STOP" lists, "Common Rationalizations"
tables, the verification Gate Function, and the MANDATORY red/green verify
steps). Paraphrasing them measurably weakens their effect, so they are not
paraphrased.

